| S1 | Registered sender gives a valid account number | Verification | Aligned | OTP to the mobile registered with the loan | Account no. + sender must be an active contact of that account + OTP; scope bound to one account | Verification subflow · LMS · OTP · Policy gateway | — | — |
| S2 | Sender's number differs from the registered number | Verification | Gap | Ask for the loan number, then send the OTP to the number on record | Sender must be an ACTIVE contact linked to the account; otherwise a uniform reply and no OTP | Verification subflow | Borrowers writing from a second phone can't self-serve. The dataset's ALTERNATE_NUMBER cases (about 8%) expect an OTP to the registered number. | Pick one rule. If the architecture rule stays, update the catalogue reply and the dataset labels. |
| S3 | Wrong OTP three times | Verification | Aligned | 30-minute pause + helpline | 3 attempts, 5-minute validity, 30-minute lock + helpline | OTP · Policy gateway | — | — |
